tting down for interviews to  discuss their new show when they sat  down with idris elba for the recent  interview they went into some of the  details about how their relationship  started according to george rr martin he  said it all started about three years  ago when hbo knew game of thrones was  ending this was when they knew they  wanted to move forward with a successor  show as you can imagine george rr martin  gave them several different ideas for a  new show and one of those ideas centered  around house targaryen and what happened  during the dance of the dragons when all  of this first started happening he said  hbo already had other writers in mind  some of those writers did not get very  far some of them got considerably far  and did good work but they did  eventually find themselves without a  writer and one day when george met with  ryan condo at the four seasons he  thought hey you would be great for this  not only had ryan read all of his novels  about westeros but according to george  he said ryan knew a lot about fantasy in  general he goes on to say now i have to  admit i'm not the most subjective guy in  this discussion i'm the author of the  original source material when you get a  writer who is hired to do an adaptation  but is not familiar with the original  material in some cases they hire someone  who doesn't even like the original  material and you have this language in  hollywood you will hear some of these  writers say i'm gonna make it my own i  have my own vision for this and that  sort of thing  not even discussing my work but  discussing myself as a viewer as a  consumer of things if i go to see the  great gatsby i don't want someone else's  version on the great gatsby i don't want  them to make it their own i won scott's  fitzgerald brought to life in front of  my face  now unfortunately you don't always get  that so to be able to work with someone  like ryan not just that he knew my books  the fact that he knew fantasy and love  fantasy was a big thing for me now if  this doesn't get you excited then i  don't know what will  according to george r martin it honestly  does sound like ryan will make a very  faithful adaptation it sounds like he's  saying ryan will make it exactly how the  author wanted it to be in fact this is  essentially what ryan says as well  during the same interview ryan said so  for me it was a trust building exercise  and the way miguel and i went into this  was as fans of the original show so what  we're all trying to do is create the  thing that we as fans would want to see  for me as a fan that meant a very  faithful adaptation so i was very lucky  in this case i had george's ear i shared  every outline that i wrote with him for  the first episode and every draft for  the pilot i wrote and then once that  started getting going and hbo was happy  i think george was happy and knew where  the story was heading and how he wanted  to move forward with the rest of the  season so that's what i really try to do  i basically made sure he was getting as  much information as i could then we  eventually wrote a series bible and he  came to los angeles to join us and heard  how all of that was unfolding so i think  at every step of the way he always knew  where the story was going so with me it  was always making sure he was involved  and keeping his eyes on it as much as i  could because i felt like if george  blessed this and said it was good or if  we debated on something and it's not the  thing he wanted we would find a solution  then i felt like i had done my job as  the author of the adaptation we did have  some healthy debates during the early  stages of developing house of the dragon  mostly about how the show would be  structured it involved a deep and  introspective look into how the material  that you wouldn't necessarily have to do  if you were just reading or discussing  it as a history book if you've read fire  and blood then you would know that it's  one guy archmaester gildane having to  sift through three other guys who all  have an incomplete account on the  history of what happened hoping to  figure out what actually happened  because we're telling the objective  version of this story we had to make  decisions about if this was going to  happen and how that was going to happen  alright so as you can see with the  interview it sounds like they are making  as faithful of an adaptation as you can  make given that they are adapting a fake  history book that does have several  different versions of the same events  if you've read fire and blood then you  know it's not structured like george's  other novels and a song of ice and fire  unfortunately fire and blood doesn't  have very much dialogue so that's  something ryan and the other writers  will have to do on their own  not only that but like i said there are  several different accounts on the same  event so they will have to decide on  whose version of these events they will  follow it will be very interesting to  see how all of this will unfold at the  end of the day they have a very good  outline because george rr martin had  already basically established what  happened during a lot of the major  events during the dance of the dragons  he has already laid out who will live  who will die and who will be seated on  the iron throne so we already know it  will have a great ending in the sense  that it won't feel like it has any holes  one thing i do know is we will find out  exactly how good house of the dragon is  in less than three months the day we  have all been waiting for is finally  almost here i have faith that ryan will  deliver a great show it honestly sounds  like that's what he wants to do for the  fans i think he also wants to do this  for george rr martin i don't think he  wants to let him down either he has been  a fan of his for several decades now so  i doubt he wants to do something that  might negatively affect how the fans  will look at his body of work either way  we will see soon enough  as always i want to thank all of you for  watching this video also don't forget to  subscribe if you would like to enter to  win george rr martin's fire and blood  vol 1.  good luck and have a great day i will  see all of you back here very soon for  my next video  bye  [Music]  you

